  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"SECRETO started when María Luisa's father dies, receiving all his belongings. Among these was a series of letters that her father had written to a psychiatrist in Chile during his exile in Peru. In the letters, she found a secret that her father kept until the day of her death. In the attempt to understand the reasons that motivated her father to hide this secret, María Luisa decides to open the question collectively through this work. That was how she exposed her father's secret inside an airmail envelope (which were the envelopes in which her father's letters arrived during the exile), inviting the audience that if they wanted to read that secret, they should leave their own. As a result, untold secrets will find themselves suddenly revealed." -- https://www.printedmatter.org/catalog/61099/</subfield>
  </datafield>
